really  usable on all of the styles that I would  like them to be usable in but yeah one  of the other things which I wanted to  get into of course are the windows on  this building and I wasn't really sure  how many of the windows I really wanted  to burn the end I ended up with having  two in the front there and two in the  back with like slightly different  distances between them which is a little  bit awkward but I kind of do like the  effects and the way that it looks in the  end and slightly more simple windows on  the tower and that should finish off  basically the rest of the building and  finally I wanted to do what I can't stop  doing and I might want to stop doing  this at some point in the future because  I am definitely going to overuse those  pieces  adding those roof pieces the the golden  roof trims on top of the roof here which  is just I know I use it a lot it's just  something which I really love and I've  tried some different fences on top of  the roofs to get the same kind of effect  but none of them really have that golden  texture and well an almost fantasy feel  to it either that this one has another  final touches and details to make the  building come alive as you can see it is  now a cosmic cow milk shake shop and I'm  adding a bunch of window boxes to add a  bit of foliage to the building make it  look a bit more inviting and that more  or less finishes this building and I  think it's time to move on to the next  one alright so the next building is  going to be one very small and simple  building and it's it's kind of like the  counterpart of the very small and simple  building on the other side as well just  two squares wide and a very simple hip  roof and a very simple corner  underneath it as well I'm just plopping  some random windows on it I have to be  honest this is pretty much just a fellow  building in every sense of the word I  just needed to get this space filled up  and to get three buildings in this would  have been way too tight but to get one  building in this space wouldn't really  fit since it would be way too large of a  building so I'm just getting this very  small building into this corner so that  we can work on the next building which  is gonna catch a bit more attention it's  gonna be a bit larger and in a style  which I haven't really done so far in  the park and he'll which I haven't  really done that often at all we're  gonna be building a quick English Tudor  kind of townhouse on this side here with  like some dough is very dark brown  archways underneath it and on the real  Tudor part with all of the frame work  we're gonna have some white stucco and  black framework which is gonna be very  dense and have all of these large roof  shapes on top of it as well so I'm  getting the gallery in there I'm playing  with the roof for a little bit I figured  it would be best to get that steep roof  in all the way since it has that very  steep sort of curved angle that I wanted  to go for and make a bit of a custom  dormer kind of roof gable that sticks  out on the front to get some windows  that really pop out of the building and  that's basically the general shape of it  it's pretty flat building but it's still  made out of two separate buildings to be  able to have there the forms that comes  out a bit more than rest of the building  and the rest of the framework is just  again it's very easy to do and I haven't  really looked up any kind of Tudor  references I might have missed some like  typical to the framing and done some  things wrong in this case which if I did  always feel free to call me out on it um  but I was just kind of going for the  general Tudor kind of atmosphere in this  case which meant a lot of very very  dense frame work much more dense than I  have with all of the Alpine building so  far the black colour in there and some  of the very gothic looking windows as  well and I've tried  but it doesn't really work outs to get  some of those to the frame works in  there because to the frameworks they  often have curves and like very specific  kind of details like to the roses in  them and it practically impossible to  really do that there's probably a way to  do it but in this case I couldn't really  be bothered to try it so I just got a  few very simple diamonds in there almost  like there is actually to the roses and  the rest of the building is just low  very heavy dense framework and that  should finish that off quite nicely and  I think I remember making this yeah this  is the information kind of building  since it is right at the entrance and  it's not the most like visible thing  like burgers or milkshakes which you  want to have as visible as you can  because you do need to make a buck out  of them and well that's how capitalism  works but we can get a bit of an  information thing in here close to the  entrance and not too much in in the line  of sight but still in a way that you can  I quickly go to as you get into the park  so very quick information booth in here  should finish off the may treat and  final things that I wanted to do is to  get in a few of these planters that I  have on the other side trying to make  all of the paths work as symmetrical as  I can and a bunch of scenery over here  as well pretty much in the same way as  the other side a few barrels here a few  like pots and urns there and a whole  bunch of planters and that should finish  off the Main Street so that's it for  today thank you guys for watching and  I'll leave you with some cinematic shots  [Music]  [Music]
 

